# Students' Long-Term Evaluation of Introductory Courses.

**Authors:** Arnold, J. David, And Others

## Abstract
Students evaluated the educational applications of introductory courses. Social science courses had the highest average rating, followed by introductory psychology, arts/humanities courses, and natural science courses, respectively. Application items rated as most helpful were understanding yourself, understanding others, and coping with problems. (RM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ330547

